  "body": "## Summary\n\nReplaces this app's bespoke auth (MSAL frontend → Microsoft ID token → shared HS256 JWT) with delegated auth to [auth.romaine.life](https://github.com/nelsong6/auth). Pattern-proof PR for the same migration coming to plant-agent, investing, house-hunt, and fzt-frontend.\n\n**Before:** Frontend uses MSAL to get a Microsoft ID token → POSTs it to `/auth/microsoft/login` → backend verifies against Microsoft JWKS, upserts a Cosmos user record, issues a self-signed JWT with the shared `api-jwt-signing-secret` → frontend stores it in localStorage.\n\n**After:** Frontend redirects to `auth.romaine.life/api/auth/sign-in/social/microsoft?callbackURL=...`. After the Microsoft dance, the auth service sets a session cookie scoped to `.romaine.life`. Frontend fetches `auth.romaine.life/api/auth/token` (cookie auto-attached), gets an RS256 JWT, stores in localStorage, sends as `Bearer`. Backend verifies via `auth.romaine.life/api/auth/jwks` using `jose`'s `createRemoteJWKSet` + `jwtVerify`.\n\n### Files\n\n**Deleted:**\n- [`backend/microsoft-routes.js`](backend/microsoft-routes.js) — entire Microsoft token-exchange + JWT issuance moves to the auth service\n- [`frontend/src/auth/msal.js`](frontend/src/auth/msal.js) — MSAL gone\n\n**Rewritten:**\n- [`backend/auth.js`](backend/auth.js) — `jsonwebtoken`+`jwks-rsa` → `jose` (`createRemoteJWKSet` + `jwtVerify`)\n- [`backend/config.js`](backend/config.js) — drops `api-jwt-signing-secret` KV fetch and Microsoft client-ID enumeration; now only reads `cosmos_db_endpoint` from App Configuration\n- [`frontend/src/auth/AuthContext.jsx`](frontend/src/auth/AuthContext.jsx) — on-mount JWT fetch from auth service, silent refresh 60 s before `exp`, `signIn`/`signOut` redirect helpers. Same `useAuth()` shape as before so callers don't change.\n\n**Trimmed:**\n- [`backend/server.js`](backend/server.js) — drops Microsoft routes mount\n- [`backend/package.json`](backend/package.json) — out: `jsonwebtoken`, `jwks-rsa`, `@azure/keyvault-secrets`; in: `jose`\n- [`frontend/package.json`](frontend/package.json) — out: `@azure/msal-browser`\n- [`frontend/src/api/client.js`](frontend/src/api/client.js), [`frontend/src/components/UserProfile.jsx`](frontend/src/components/UserProfile.jsx) — swap `loginWithMicrosoft` for the new redirect/`signIn`\n- [`Dockerfile`](Dockerfile) — drop `VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID` build arg\n- [`.github/workflows/build-and-deploy.yaml`](.github/workflows/build-and-deploy.yaml) — drop the App Configuration fetch that fed that build arg\n- [`k8s/deployment.yaml`](k8s/deployment.yaml) — drop `KEY_VAULT_URL` env (no Key Vault reads from the pod anymore)\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Build and Deploy workflow succeeds (image builds without the MS client ID build arg)\n- [ ] After ArgoCD rolls the new image, hit `workout.romaine.life` while signed in to auth.romaine.life → should auto-fetch a JWT and load with user identity\n- [ ] Click Sign In while signed out → redirects to auth.romaine.life Microsoft flow → returns to workout.romaine.life signed in\n- [ ] Sign Out → cookie cleared on auth.romaine.life, localStorage cleared on workout.romaine.life, user back to anonymous\n- [ ] Admin tab visibility honors `user.role === 'admin'` — currently `member` until the auth service's user record has `role` updated (see below)\n- [ ] After signing in, API requests to `workout.romaine.life/api/*` carry the JWT as `Bearer` and the backend's JWKS verification accepts them\n\n## Notes for sequencing\n\n- **User data:** existing Cosmos records keyed by `microsoft|\u003cMS-sub\u003e` won't match the new JWT `sub` (which is Better Auth's random user.id). For a single-user system this is a fresh start. Old records will just sit there unreferenced until you clean them up.\n- **Admin role:** after first sign-in, the auth service's `user` table has `role = 'user'` (default). Mark yourself admin with a one-time SQL against the auth Postgres pod: `UPDATE \"user\" SET role='admin' WHERE email='nelson@romaine.life';`. The JWT will pick it up on next token fetch.\n- **Old microsoft-login SPA redirects** (`https://workout.romaine.life/`) remain on the [`microsoft_login` app reg](https://github.com/nelsong6/infra-bootstrap/blob/main/tofu/oauth.tf) for now. After all 5 apps migrate, a final infra-bootstrap PR drops the SPA list entirely.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
